  },
  "causes": {
    "shellcheck-embedded/SC1003": "A command quoted for `sh -c` inside a script that is itself quoted for `sh -c` (a step's `run` in the set-up, through shell::quote twice) reads as `\\'` inside single quotes to shellcheck's heuristic: the shell reads the quoting as written, the step's own command, and SC1003 is shellcheck's info, not an error.",
    "shellcheck-embedded/SC1091": "The set-up reads `/var/lib/isoloom/secrets.env`, which Terraform writes into the machine from its sensitive variables: there is no such file to follow where the module is checked.",
    "shellcheck-embedded/SC2015": "`<steps> && … || { echo 'failed: …'; exit 1; }` is the set-up's step form on purpose: the failure mark runs when any command of the chain fails, which is what the `||` is for.",
    "shellcheck-embedded/SC2016": "A secret's delivery runs `env NAME=<value> sh -c '… \"$v\" …'`: the single quotes keep `$v` for the inner shell, which sets it, so nothing is meant to expand in the outer one."
  },
